# Dance of the Dead: Bot1 kills its own Ornithopter with Cut Down and casts Dance of the Dead ({1}{B}) on the card in its
# graveyard (the enchant ability allows only a creature card in a graveyard, CR 303.4a: not the Ornithopter on the
# battlefield, not the Cut Down card). The Aura's enters ability puts the Ornithopter onto the battlefield tapped (CR
# 110.5b) and attaches the Aura to it, a 1/3 under "+1/+1". It doesn't untap in Bot1's untap steps (CR 502.3). In Bot1's
# upkeep on turn 3 Bot1 holds only two white mana, which can't pay {1}{B}; on turn 5 Bot1 may pay and declines, and the
# Ornithopter stays tapped; on turn 7 Bot1 pays exactly {1}{B} with a Swamp and a Mox Pearl, leaving the other Mox Pearl
# untapped, and the Ornithopter untaps (CR 118.12).

